                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove full revolutions; the remaining half-turn preserves tangent.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Remove the full revolutions, then use $\\tan(180^{\\circ}+\\theta)=\\tan\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\bigl(180(2n+1)^{\\circ}+\\theta\\bigr)&=\\tan(360n^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ}+\\theta)\\\\\\tan\\bigl(180(2n+1)^{\\circ}+\\theta\\bigr)&=\\tan(180^{\\circ}+\\theta)\\\\\\tan\\bigl(180(2n+1)^{\\circ}+\\theta\\bigr)&=\\tan\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nThese equalities hold where tangent is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
